#: content/for/travelers.md:47
msgid "KDE Itinerary"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:49
msgid ""
"KDE Itinerary is a digital travel assistant that protects your privacy. It "
"makes collecting all the information about your travel inside a single "
"application easy and straightforward. KDE Itinerary is available for [Plasma "
"Mobile](https://plasma-mobile.org/) and Android."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:57
msgid "Store your reservations"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:59
msgid ""
"Store all the information about your reservations in Itinerary. This "
"includes QR-codes, check-in times, arrivial times, real-time delays, seat "
"reservations, coach layout, and more."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:61
msgid ""
"Itinerary supports train, bus and flight bookings, as well as hotel, "
"restaurant, event and rental car reservations. Traveling in a group? Not a "
"problem, Itinerary supports multi-traveler bookings."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:69
msgid ""
"Itinerary automatically extracts booking data from various input formats. "
"It's all performed locally on **your** device and your data is not sent to "
"any remote servers."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:71
msgid ""
"This works best when using [KMail](https://kontact.kde.org/components/"
"kmail/) to extract tickets from your email and then [KDE Connect](https://"
"kdeconnect.kde.org) to transfer tickets to your phone. This also works great "
"with [Nextcloud Mail](https://apps.nextcloud.com/apps/mail) and [DavDroid]"
"(https://f-droid.org/en/packages/at.bitfire.davdroid/) to sync your tickets "
"from [Nextcloud](https://nextcloud.com/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:73
msgid ""
"![KMail ticket extraction showing a train trip from Berlin to Tübingen]"
"(kmail.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:79
msgid "Add your connections"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:81
msgid ""
"Aside from finding reservations automatically in your email, Itinerary lets "
"you add train trips manually to your journey, find alternative connections "
"if your train is cancelled, or, for some providers, import your train trip "
"directly from your reservation number."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:87
msgid "Find your way"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:89
msgid ""
"Powered by [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org), the indoor map at "
"train stations or airports can be a life saver. Use Itinerary to locate your "
"platform is, and, if you have seat reservation and the train layout is "
"available, it can even show you exactly which platform section is best for "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:91
msgid ""
"![Train station map in KDE Itinerary, highlighting relevant platform "
"sections.](https://www.volkerkrause.eu/assets/posts/139/kde-itinerary-"
"platform-section-highlighting.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:93
msgid ""
"The indoor map also shows you which shops and resturantes are currently "
"open, which elevator is broken (yet again!), where the toilets are and where "
"the correct exit is."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:99
msgid "Real time"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:101
msgid ""
"It is rare that a train or bus departs or arrives on time. Itinerary keeps "
"you updated when delays are announced."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:103
msgid ""
"On supported train and long distance buses, Itinerary will also use the "
"onboard APIs to fetch the current live status of the vehicle and keep you "
"updated on your current position and any announcements."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:109
msgid "Arianna"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:111
msgid ""
"Arianna is an excellent ebook reader that lets you read your favorite books "
"while traveling. Arianna will track your reading progress and classify your "
"books by genre and author automatically."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:116
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Arianna](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/arianna/reader.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:122
msgid "Kasts"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:124
msgid ""
"Enjoy listening to podcasts on the move with Kasts! Subscribe to your "
"favorite podcasts and get updated as soon as a new episode is out."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:128
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Kasts](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/kasts/kasts-desktop."
"png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:130
msgid ""
"Kasts is also available on Android and [Plasma Mobile](https://plasma-mobile."
"org)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:142
msgid "KGeoTag"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:144
msgid ""
"KGeoTag is a geotagging program. It lets you tag your images with "
"geocoordinates by matching them to a corresponding GPX track or by manually "
"setting them by drag and dropping the images, or entering the coordinates by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:146
msgid ""
"It is very helpful in combination with [KPhotoAlbum](https://www.kphotoalbum."
"org/) or [Digikam](https://www.digikam.org/) when you want to organize your "
"photo collection after your trip and then visualize all the locations you "
"visited."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:150
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of KGeoTag showing a track on a map with some image preview "
"allong the track](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/kgeotag/kgeotag_shadow.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:156
msgid "Marble"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:158
msgid ""
"Explore the world with Marble. Marble contains a huge collection of maps "
"that let you travel all over the globe from your desktop. Visit remote "
"places via detailed satellite images, travel the world before the discovery "
"of America, and check out the average temperature and precipitation in "
"winter and summer in other countries."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:160
msgid ""
"Marble also allows you to bookmark your favorite locations and lets you find "
"your way thanks to its routing algorithm and OpenStreetMap powered maps."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:164
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Kasts](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/marble/marble-world."
"png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:170
msgid "Other open source apps for you"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:172
msgid ""
"Here are some other applications from other open source communities that "
"will make your travels fun."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid "KDE for Windows 10 Exiles"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid "Upgrade your software, not your computer"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Plasma is a Desktop"
msgid "Plasma is easy"
msgstr "ပလက်စမာသည် ဒက်စ်တော့ပ်ဖြစ်သည်"

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid ""
"Plasma immediately feels like home. With its launch menu for apps in the "
"bottom left-hand corner; workspace where you can drop apps, files and "
"folders; and tray for important widgets, you will instantly locate "
"everything you need."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid "Plasma adapts to you"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid ""
"Plasma lets you move things around and change their looks to your liking. "
"You can make Plasma look and feel like Windows (any version), macOS, or "
"something with no equivalent in the closed source world. Make Plasma your "
"own and [show us what you did](https://discuss.kde.org/t/share-your-"
"desktop/490/504)!"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid "Plasma comes free of licensing costs"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:0
msgid ""
"It doesn't matter if you are installing Plasma on one computer or fifty—no-"
"one is going to bill you for it. All our code is open source and KDE itself "
"is a non-profit run by volunteers."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:26
msgid "Your computer is toast"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:28
msgid ""
"Running Windows 10 on your computer? On October 14 Microsoft wants to turn "
"it into junk."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:30
msgid ""
"It may seem like it continues to work after that date for a bit, but when "
"Microsoft stops support for Windows 10, your perfectly good computer will be "
"officially obsolete."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:32
msgid ""
"<img src=\"e-waste01.jpg\" class=\"img-fluid kirigami-devices\" alt="
"\"Electronic junk covered in grimy dust.\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:36
msgid ""
"Windows 10 will degrade as more and more bugs come to light. With nobody to "
"correct them, you risk being hacked. Your data, identity, and control over "
"your device could be stolen."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:38
msgid ""
"New versions of your apps will not run, but Microsoft will still block you "
"from upgrading to the next version of Windows until you [buy the new "
"computer they decide](https://www.forbes.com/sites/zakdoffman/2025/01/18/"
"microsofts-forced-upgrade-new-warning-for-450-million-windows-pc-owners/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:40
msgid ""
"You will be forced to spend your hard-earned cash and will be unwillingly "
"polluting the earth and water as your old machine rots in a landfill. The "
"air will also be polluted with the emissions that come from manufacturing "
"and shipping a new device you don't really need."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:42
msgid ""
"Even if you agree to this tech extortion now, in a few years time, they will "
"do it again as they have [done many times](https://www.wsj.com/articles/"
"SB10001424127887323936804578229682529360570) in [the past](https://www."
"techradar.com/news/software/operating-systems/microsoft-defends-vista-"
"against-green-party-141019)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:44
msgid "But things don't have to be this way..."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:50
msgid "What you can do"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:52
msgid ""
"Upgrade the smart way! Keep the machine you've got and switch to **Linux** "
"and **[Plasma](https://kde.org/plasma-desktop/)**."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:54
msgid ""
"Linux can give new life to your laptop. Combined with [KDE's Plasma desktop]"
"(https://kde.org/plasma-desktop/), you get all the advantages of the safety, "
"stability and hi tech of Linux, with all the features of a beautiful, modern "
"and powerful graphic environment."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:58
msgid ""
"And it'll work on the machine you already have. Even machines that are 10, "
"15 years old [can happily run Plasma](https://tube.kockatoo.org/w/"
"g9p72nNRHi6bArN4ABtSQM), a modern, safe operating system that won't let you "
"down."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:60
msgid ""
"You can get Plasma from many Linux flavours ([here are a few](https://kde."
"org/distributions/))."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:62
msgid ""
"You can install Linux yourself—installing Linux is not as hard as it used to "
"be, but you must read the instructions to do so very carefully!"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:64
msgid ""
"Or, if you have never installed an operating system before, we have [events]"
"(https://endof10.org/events/) and [places](https://endof10.org/places/) all "
"over the world. You can go with your machine and someone will help you out."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:70
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Plasma"
msgid "Why Plasma"
msgstr "ပလက်စမာ"

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:70
msgid ""
"Here are some reasons to choose Plasma as your next upgrade from Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:76
msgid "Plasma is powerful"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:78
msgid ""
"Looks are not everything. Plasma also packs **dozens of useful features** "
"that make it a pleasure to use."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:80
msgid ""
"Did you ever feel constrained by just one desktop? Linux users regularly use "
"four! But you can have more if you like—and arrange them on cube."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:84
msgid ""
"For the technically minded, need to connect to your web server to update "
"your blog, or your cloud to upload photos, or even your software repository "
"for development? Just pop open [Dolphin](https://apps.kde.org/dolphin/), "
"Plasma's file explorer, and use its connectivity tools, that include FTP/SSH "
"clients, cloud integration software, Git/SVN/Mercurial, and more. For more "
"on how Plasma makes your work easier, check out our [For Developers page]"
"(https://kde.org/for/developers/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:88
msgid ""
"Need to connect to your office machine to send of a report or to help out a "
"colleague with an issue while stuck at home? Plasma has **desktop sharing** "
"system baked in."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:90
msgid ""
"There are many other desktop environments for Linux. Check out [GNOME]"
"(http://www.gnome.org/), [XFCE](https://xfce.org/), [Mate](https://mate-"
"desktop.com/), [Cinnamon](https://projects.linuxmint.com/cinnamon/), [LXQt]"
"(https://lxqt.github.io/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:96
msgid "Get ready"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:98
msgid ""
"You may be wondering if you will still be able to do what you did on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:100
msgid ""
"Linux does take some getting used to after years of using Windows, and you "
"may need different programs to work and play."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:102
msgid "But there are three tricks that will make the transition easier:"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:104
msgid "1. Rely on the Free Software community"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:106
msgid ""
"... And ask a lot of questions! Linux users are a proud bunch and will "
"happily guide you so you quickly become at home."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:108
msgid ""
"This works for when you want to install Linux! The [EndOf10](https://endof10."
"org/) campaign provides a list of organizations and live events where you "
"can go for help."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:110
msgid ""
"[Here are some more places](https://kde.org/support/) run by the KDE "
"Community where new users are not only welcome, but encouraged to "
"participate:"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:112
msgid ""
"[KDE Discuss](https://discuss.kde.org/) (free registration required if you "
"want to ask questions)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:113
msgid ""
"[KDE User Help](https://matrix.to/#/#kde:kde.org) chat room (requires free "
"registration)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:114
msgid ""
"[KDE mailing](https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde) (free subscription)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:117
msgid "2. Do not expect the same things you would use in Windows"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:119
msgid ""
"... but instead look for the programs that will do the same job on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:121
msgid ""
"Many Linux systems come with the most commonly used software pre-installed. "
"This allows you to hit the ground running: [Firefox](https://www.mozilla.org/"
"en-US/firefox/new/) is there for web browsing; [LibreOffice](https://www."
"libreoffice.org/) comes with the programs you need to write documents, "
"create spreadsheets, design presentations, etc.; and [Okular](https://okular."
"kde.org/) lets you open, sign and annotate PDFs (and many other types of "
"documents)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:125
msgid ""
"**Note that these are not demos or bloatware!** They are complete programs "
"with all their features for you to enjoy and use forever. That is what Free "
"Software is all about."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:127
msgid "But when you need more specialized applications..."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:129
msgid "3. Trust your package manager"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:131
msgid ""
"Linux package managers provide you with a BIG catalog of software. Plasma "
"comes with [Discover](https://apps.kde.org/discover/), an app store/software "
"manager."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:133
msgid ""
"It contains mostly free and open software, and an intuitive search function. "
"If you don't know the name of the application you need, type in some "
"keywords related to what want it to do in the _Search_ box and Discover will "
"suggest something."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:137
msgid ""
"Services like [Flatpak](https://flatpak.org/) provide extra software which "
"can also be installed from Discover."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:139
msgid "What you should not do"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:141
msgid ""
"Don't go hunting for software on the web! Linux is all about keeping "
"yourself safe and the resources explained above do that."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:149
msgid "What will you miss"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:151
msgid ""
"Keeping all your files and folders will require some planning, but it is not "
"hard. Get yourself an external hard disk you can plug into a USB port and "
"dump all the stuff you want to save on that. You will have no problem "
"reading it from Plasma later on."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:153
msgid ""
"As for the rest, for most of the good stuff you will be covered. Most "
"hardware (WiFi/Bluetooth and video cards, even drawing tablets, etc.) will "
"be recognized and configured by the system automatically—no more hunting for "
"drivers."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:155
msgid "But you can say goodbye to all the bad stuff:"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:157
msgid "No viruses or virus-related scams"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:159
msgid ""
"Viruses for Linux are pretty much unknown, so you can forget that worry. You "
"won't be seeing any of those scam antivirus popups either."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:161
msgid ""
"<div class=\"row\">\n"
"  <div class=\"col-12 col-lg-6\">\n"
"    <h3 class=\"mt-0\">No more ads</h3>\n"
"    <p class=\"text-left\">It may seem that you got Windows for free, but it "
"definitely comes at a cost. Microsoft routinely injects advertisements into "
"your desktop, in free apps, in your apps launch menu, in the help and "
"guides, even in your file browser. They will go as far as shamelessly "
"displaying full screen ads for upcoming software. These ads eat up you "
"bandwidth, leach power from your computer, degrade the performance of the "
"operating system and in general just interfere with your day. There is "
"nothing like that in Plasma.</p>\n"
"    <h3 class=\"mt-0\">No spyware leaking your activity</h3>\n"
"    <p class=\"text-left\">Say goodbye to hidden processes  spying on every "
"word you type in every app. And no more uploading of your documents to "
"someone else's cloud to train their AI behind your back, stealing your work "
"for someone else's profit. KDE is charity run by volunteers, not a company. "
"We have no commercial interests. We also have no interest in your personal "
"data and will fiercely help you protect it.</p>\n"
"  </div>\n"
"  <div class=\"col-12 col-lg-6\">\n"
"    <img src=\"steve_ballmer_sells_Windows.jpg\" class=\"img-fluid kirigami-"
"devices\" alt=\"\" />\n"
"  </div>\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:173
msgid "No forced updates"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:175
msgid ""
"When updates are available, you will see a discreet icon in your tray or a "
"pop up will appear. You chose when you want to update, now, another day,... "
"whenever you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:177
msgid "No surprise app changes"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:179
msgid ""
"You pick what apps open your files. You will be always fully in control "
"which does what and when. Once you pick an app to open a certain type of "
"files or as your default web browser, that is what the system will stick "
"with. Plasma makes you the boss."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:181
msgid "No forced registrations, subscriptions, hidden costs"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:183
msgid ""
"You don't need a Microsoft account, or register with any other company, or "
"pay a subscription for anything that doesn't need it."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:185
msgid ""
"In fact, unless you are doing something that requires a connection to the "
"Internet, like uploading pic to the cloud, posting to social media, or "
"streaming a movie, Plasma doesn't even need to be connected to the Internet."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/w10-exiles.md:187
msgid ""
"Everything that can be done locally on your computer, is done locally on "
"your computer, and nothing outside your box needs to know anything about it."
msgstr ""

