msgid ""
"<p style=\"font-size: smaller;\">\n"
"<b>Note:</b><br />\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/international.md:40
msgid ""
"Our policy regarding the sites listed above is simple: If somebody goes "
"through the trouble of creating a KDE website, then we will include it in "
"this list. Furthermore, we will <em>not</em> override the site creator's "
"preference for what to call their geographical area (e.g., calling the "
"Taiwan site \"Taiwan\" instead of \"China\")."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/international.md:46
msgid "</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:0
msgid "KDE Mailing Lists"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:6
msgid ""
"The KDE mailing lists are one of the main communication channels in the KDE "
"Community. This is a list of general mailing lists to give a quick overview. "
"For application specific lists, please see the <a href=\"../../applications/"
"\">application's page</a>. For a complete overview, see the <a href="
"\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo\">full list of all mailing lists</a>."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:9
msgid "General user lists"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:11
msgid ""
"<b>kde</b> - for KDE users with questions strictly about KDE applications "
"<br />(<a href=\"http://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde\">subscribe kde</"
"a>, <a href=\"http://lists.kde.org/?l=kde&amp;r=1&amp;w=2\">archive of kde</"
"a>)"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:15
msgid ""
"<b>kde-announce</b> - announcements of new KDE releases, security "
"announcements, and notification of new KDE applications (very low traffic) "
"<br />(<a href=\"http://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-announce"
"\">subscribe kde-announce</a>, <a href=\"http://lists.kde.org/?l=kde-"
"announce&amp;r=1&amp;w=2\">archive of kde-announce</a>)"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:19
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Development Tools"
msgid "General development lists"
msgstr "ပရိုဂရမ်မာသုံးကိရိယာများ"

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:21
msgid ""
"<b>kde-devel</b> - for application developers (both applications in central "
"KDE packages and contributed applications <br />(<a href=\"http://mail.kde."
"org/mailman/listinfo/kde-devel\">subscribe kde-devel</a>, <a href=\"http://"
"lists.kde.org/?l=kde-devel&amp;r=1&amp;w=2\">archive of kde-devel</a>)"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:25
msgid ""
"<b>kde-core-devel</b> - for KDE library developers. The discussions on this "
"list are limited at KDE libraries development, git and other central "
"development issues. <br />(<a href=\"http://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/"
"kde-core-devel\">subscribe kde-core-devel</a>, <a href=\"http://lists.kde."
"org/?l=kde-core-devel&amp;r=1&amp;w=2\">archive of kde-core-devel</a>)"
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:30
msgid ""
"To <b>Subscribe</b>: Either use the above links and use the mailman "
"interface, or send a mail to <i>list-name</i>&#x2d;r&#101;&#00113;&#117;"
"e&#x73;&#116;&#064;k&#0100;&#101;&#0046;org with <i>subscribe your-email-"
"address</i> in the subject of the message. Please write your real email "
"address instead of the plain \"<i>your-email-address</i>\" words, and the "
"name of the list instead of the \"<i>list-name</i>\" words. Leave the body "
"of the message empty. Do not include a signature or other stuff which might "
"confuse the mail server which processes your request."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:39
msgid ""
"To <b>Unsubscribe</b>: Either use the above links and use the mailman "
"interface, or send a mail to <i>list-name</i>&#x2d;r&#x65;q&#117;e&#115;"
"&#116;&#x40;kde&#x2e;&#111;&#114;g with <i>unsubscribe your-email-address</"
"i> in the subject of the message. Please replace \"<i>your-email-address</i>"
"\" with the email address you did use for the subscription, and \"<i>list-"
"name</i>\" with the name of the list you subscribed to. Leave the body of "
"the message empty. Do not include a signature or other stuff which might "
"confuse the mail server which processes your request."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:48
msgid ""
"<b>Notes</b>:<br /> Please do not use HTML to send your request because it "
"makes it difficult for our mail server to process your request. If the "
"subscription address is identical to the address you are posting from you "
"may omit the address in the subject line."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:54
msgid ""
"Contact addresses for developers can be found in the documentation of their "
"individual applications."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/mailinglists.md:57
msgid ""
"The KDE Project consists of a loose affiliation of developers, writers, "
"translators, artists and other contributors from around the world. Views "
"expressed on the mailing lists are, unless explicitly stated otherwise, the "
"views of the poster only, do not reflect the views of the KDE Project and "
"may or may not reflect the views of other KDE contributors."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Thank You"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Fosshost"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donates virtual servers"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"We use a virtual server provided by Fosshost to run WebSVN and LXR, and "
"another to host privacy-respecting analytics and statistics of our websites "
"and software."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "DigitalOcean"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Sponsors free credits on their cloud platform"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"We use a DigitalOcean droplet (virtual private server) to host one of our "
"repository mirrors, and part of the KDE neon infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "CDN77"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of Content Distribution Network services"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"CDN77 is used to globally distribute the common images, stylesheets, "
"javascript and other elements which are used on numerous KDE websites, "
"enhancing performance and improving access to our sites in the process."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "stepping stone GmbH"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of a virtual server"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Mason is used to run an Anonymous Git server, providing access to KDE Git "
"repositories over git:// and http://"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Ange Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Sponsors a hosted server"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Ange Optimization has sponsored a server hosted by Hetzner. This server was "
"used as a build node for the KDE CI system prior to it being retired."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Gärtner Datensysteme GmbH & Co. KG"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation and hosting of 3 virtual servers."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Gärtner has donated a series of virtual machines, which host Scripty and the "
"generation process for docs.kde.org as well as our server monitoring system."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Dalhousie University & ACORN"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation and hosting of a server."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Dalhousie University has donated dalca.kde.org and hosts it, with network "
"connectivity provided by ACORN. This server is used as a build node for the "
"KDE CI system."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Cloudflare"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of CDN services"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Cloudflare protects some of our sites against SQL-injections and XSS-"
"scripting. It also provides a CDN for common images, javascript and "
"stylesheets which are used on multiple sites to optimize performance."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "ClouDNS"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of DNS services"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"CloudDNS provides anycast nameservers for all our domains. Normal "
"namesevers, DDOS-protected nameservers for our important domains and also "
"GEO-ip-based nameservers for providing the right SCM-mirror in each "
"continent."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Canonical"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation and hosting of a server (cano.kde.org)"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Canonical has donated cano.kde.org and takes care of the hosting. This "
"server hosted a number of websites prior to its retirement."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "GNU/FSF"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of a virtual server (bluemchen.kde.org)"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"This server is used for a variety of tasks, including handling all "
"transactional email for KDE.org services."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "OSUOSL"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of a virtual server (stumptown.kde.org)"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"This server was used for a series of small websites prior to its retirement."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Francesco Riosa"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of a virtual server (zivo.kde.org)"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"This server was used to host our API documentation (api.kde.org) as well as "
"the English Breakfast Network (ebn.kde.org) prior to it being retired."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "EuroVPS"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of 3 servers"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid ""
"Servers provided by EuroVPS host an instance of Sentry.io as well as "
"services for producing embedded builds of KDE software, in particular using "
"Yocto."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Matrix.org Foundation"
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Donation of hosted Matrix home server."
msgstr ""

#: content/thanks/_index.md:0
msgid "Matrix instant messaging services for the community to use."
msgstr ""

